<title>USA: Owens Corning sets dividend, poison pill.</title>
<headline>Owens Corning sets dividend, poison pill.</headline>
<dateline>TOLEDO, OHIO 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Owens Corning said it declared a quarterly dividend and adopted a shareholder rights plan to guard against a hostile takeover attempt.</p>
<p>The company said it will pay a quarterly dividend of $0.0625 per share on each share of its common stock on January 15 to shareholders of record on December 31.</p>
<p>Under the shareholders plan, or poison pill, Owens Corning shareholders will get one right to buy 1/100 of a share of the company's Series A preferred stock at $190 per common share.</p>
<p>The company said it did not adopt the plan in response to any specific takeover attempts, nor was it aware of any.</p>
